s.t:
Experience of one or more of the following would be an advantage but not essential:
Recognised Project Management training;
Previous experience of providing consulting services in a multi-disciplinary engineering environment;
Commercial awareness and contract knowledge (e.g. IChemE or FIDIC);
Design experience gained from concept development and detailed engineering;
Practical experience gained from construction, commissioning, and testing;
Thermal power plant experience such as biomass power plant, waste to energy plant, gas fired power plant etc.
Energy transition technologies such as carbon capture, green hydrogen, green ammonia, power to X, etc.
Knowledge of software for thermal modelling of water/steam cycles (e.g. SteamPro).

Product Requirements and Features: Contribute to the analysis, understanding and documentation of product requirements and functionalities in collaboration with the system architect and other disciplines;
Develop and propose mechanical concepts;
Characterize the mechanical and acoustic performance requirements of the product (standards, sensitivity, frequency, surface treatment, etc.);
Characterize manufacturing, assembly and after-sales service requirements, in collaboration with operations;
Characterize the physico-mechanical properties of materials and components (geometry, stiffness, mass, thermal and fluidic effects, etc.);
Product Design: Define and perform the mechanical design of transducers and their manufacturing
Manage the technical risks of development under their responsibility;
Ensure that production cost objectives are met;
Oversee mechanical product design reviews;
Approve parts and assembly plans;
Product verification and validation: Define the validation protocol for each of the mechanical components
Ensure that the design meets product specifications;
Transfer to production: Contribute with the project manager to the planning of the work required for the transfer to production;
Provide the mechanical specifications necessary for operations and technical writing;
Ensure the updating of manufacturing documents in the PLM tool (Bill of Materials, drawings, 3D parts, etc.).

Support less experienced mechanical designers working on the same project;
Collaborate with the various stakeholders to resolve inter-departmental technical problems;
Promote cross-site work and ensure an effective and open link with counterparts in other sites
Support the introduction and optimize the use of new methods and tools according to the company's technology direction
Be involved and actively participate in the development and implementation of the culture of continuous improvement

Possess mechanical intuition to identify the physics problems of products in development;
Demonstrated experience in organizing and monitoring development work in projects;
Proficiency in mechanical design tools (SolidWorks Suite);
Have made a significant contribution to the development of commercially successful products;
Knowledge of ultrasound test and measurement applications is a plus
Knowledge of piezoelectric ceramics and materials is a plus
Machining and prototyping experience is a plus
